{"type":"text","timestamp":1790445019043,"sessionID":"ses_f212d3ba9ffeyO8eKKCixip51E","part":{"id":"prt_0ded6df8a001pb7fyqMedcp6Bj","messageID":"msg_0ded6978b0011sNHfJwruohFxF","sessionID":"ses_f212d3ba9ffeyO8eKKCixip51E","type":"text","text":"Task complete. All changes made and verified:\n\n1. **`scenes/weapon_rig.tscn`** — `WeaponEffects` keeps its existing `barrel_end`/`barrel_ray_cast` export bindings and now also sets `camera_shake_power = 0.3`.\n\n2. **`scripts/weapon_effects.gd`** — declares `signal on_shot_camera_impulse(direction: Vector3, power: float)`, adds `@export var camera_shake_power: float = 0.3`, and `fire_weapon()` computes the normalized `-BarrelRayCast` global-forward direction — since a Godot node's forward is `-basis.z`, the negative of that is `global_transform.basis.z.normalized()` — then emits the signal with the exported power.\n\n3. **`scripts/player_body.gd`** — new `apply_weapon_impulse(direction, power)` forwards to the existing `impulse_camera_with_recoil()`.\n\n4. **`scenes/main.tscn`** — added the scene connection: `on_shot_camera_impulse` from `WeaponEffects` → `PlayerBody.apply_weapon_impulse`.\n\n**Runtime verification** (headless Godot 4.4.1 against the actual scene): `camera_shake_power == 0.3`, connection resolves to `apply_weapon_impulse`, and calling `fire_weapon()` immediately produced `camera_shake_position = (0.0, 0.12, 0.09)` — backward (+Z) kick plus recoil jump, clamped by the engine's existing `camera_shake_max_power = 0.15` — and the physical camera node moved to `(0.0007, 0.029, 0.0118)`, confirming firing instantly kicks the PlayerBody camera backward. No parse errors or warnings on import.","time":{"start":1790445019018,"end":1790445019021},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_0ea6b211e6bb44d8aa66ff8a59fbcb98_msg"}}}}
